UI.GeneralControls.WaterDetail=Water is vital for life support and supplies both hydrogen and oxygen through electrolysis. Hydrogen is used in many advanced space-propulsion systems, and water is also a source of deuterium for nuclear applications. It is rare in the inner Solar System but increasingly abundant beyond the Asteroid Belt. <h>Water will be sent from Earth when production is insufficient at a Boost penalty.</h>
UI.GeneralControls.VolatilesDetail=Volatiles are reactive substances such as carbon, nitrogen, sulfur, chlorine, phosphorus, and hydrogen-bearing compounds other than water. These are critical for life support and self-sustaining space habitats, while carbon may also be fashioned into high-tech armors. Oxygen bound into silicates and oxides is not included; mineral oxygen is recovered through regolith processing, while oxygen from ice is represented by Water. <h>Volatiles will be sent from Earth when production is insufficient at a Boost penalty.</h>
